    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce0394d4_7fe58539",
        "filename": "Tethering/apishim/31/com/android/networkstack/tethering/apishim/api31/BpfCoordinatorShimImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 342,
      "author": {
        "id": 1348424
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-31T13:03:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Short answer: upstream key can\u0027t provide upstream index while calling tetherOffloadRuleRemove.\n\nHere is the interface index information what the key and value have:\nUpstream4Key: downstream index\nUpstream4Value: upstream index\nDownstream4Key: upstream index\nDownstream4Value: downstream index\n\nFor tetherOffloadRuleAdd, we could count on downstream or upstream because both key and value are sent as parameters.\ntetherOffloadRuleAdd --\u003e Upstream4Value.upstreamIndex\n---- or ----\ntetherOffloadRuleAdd --\u003e Downstream4Key.upstreamIndex\n\nFor tetherOffloadRuleRemove, we could only count on downstream because value (Upstream4Value) is not sent as parameter.\ntetherOffloadRuleRemove --\u003e Downstream4Key.upstreamIndex\n\nIf we want to count on upstream, tetherOffloadRuleRemove needs to get both key and value which is not really required by deleting entry.\n\nApproach:\n1. counting on downstream (current)\n2. counting on upstream\nneeds to pass value to tetherOffloadRuleRemove. The value is not unnecessary for deleting entry (only key is required). Building the value while deleting may be hard (need to review) because we need to make sure all elements of the value are still existing at that moment (or pass upstream index but whole value).\n3. drop counting and iterate on bpf map (original design, preferred personally) \nfor one upstream interface, mostly first rule will tell you the answer and don\u0027t need to walk through the map. That also can make the code easier and don\u0027t worry about out-of-sync problem. \n\nPlease share your thinking and any advice. Thank you",
      "parentUuid": "94250cb3_3e9dfc51",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 335,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 342,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "2fccaf5c956fc69880030b52882148905c6e8fff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
